<description>&lt;p&gt;Venezuela is coping with deadly earthquakes that have killed thousands and prompted humanitarian response, while President Nicolás Maduro and his wife have pleaded not guilty to U.S. conspiracy to torture charges and face a trial in New York. The United States has deployed Space Force electromagnetic and electronic warfare systems against Venezuela and disclosed use of space warfare weapons, mirroring actions taken in Iran, and is preparing to justify recent boat strikes on drug traffickers near Venezuelan waters. A U.S. soldier who wagered $400,000 on Maduro's removal made his first court appearance and was arrested. Two battle-related deaths were recorded in 2007, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihAFBVV95cUxPMTlvMlFLS3dOcXlXRmV3eFdaeVFlZlJ5V0xoZkFiRGw3Zm1LX3FTa3RrWUhOWlk0SzRUUzNJeGVuMVVrTkt2bzR1ZWp3by1Bb1NybkhGbUhaRmpwWTRLVU5ENnl6OFdxM0Y2YnFvV3JXb1NuY09TUHl3S0pISzh0em1aR0s?oc=5&quot;&gt;DW.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikAFBVV95cUxPSThkVlA4a1BiZmExS0k4djM2cmEwaXliX2k5eUFnLU9qM2x6X0llMkU5QjhiNWxZLVI0SzF6Ykc5aEVVTTFydjF4MzgtVHJPRU10V2tFM0prSWRDVWJiU2pUaFNlLWo0eGd3dmtwNjFZYk1HLUVreW1rMzhKUDZ2Wm9FNzFFVnZGVE51REU1aWY?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikgFBVV95cUxPSm53RDlpSVFXRjkzV1pJTkIyYlRzeFptSU1ManNGYXJnRFdmNFo2OGFOdjVxQU9UcDNmbllWMzFmbmJNV2tEc1UwQy1rWU5CYmJURnZkaUF1c1Y4UXAzV2JZNmdPdnhYcENsYmh0bXRJLTBTNFNGWUl4QjZKOHJ3QzhuZmtvcWplbGN3OVVaQXNmdw?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirwFBVV95cUxOT0UxWnM3Qk5fOS1MLVByanktMnFob0VYY3BvLVhYTU41ZWl5eEU2VE85YXlNaXZQV3lSMHI5MHhvT1hLZkMycWt2Q0RmbE9LcllPbGhHRjNRNC0tSktTNlM5UFF4d0c4clZBR3Z2aFFlUnhjNzF6WWZwQzlVNmJrNmIwc0R0TTdERGlfNHBGWmI2T2lzaDlkTHlPRG9QbW9i